./data/screening_codex_fulltext_docling_graph_direct_clean_both_targets_2026-07-10/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0054.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003121","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record describes a new model, sCellTransformer, trained from unprocessed single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data for zero-shot prediction tasks. It also states the model is pretrained with language-model objectives and predicts discretized gene expression tokens, supporting both generative and foundation-model evidence.","evidence_snippet":"\"pretrained with language model objectives\"; \"predicts about a million discretized gene expression tokens\"; \"trained from unprocessed single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data\"; \"zero-shot predictions\"; \"outperforming current foundation models\"."}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0173.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_001784","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpliceBERT is presented as a pre-trained language model for pre-mRNA splicing, but the provided evidence supports unsupervised representation learning and embeddings rather than an explicitly generative architecture. It does provide foundation-model-like evidence through pretraining on precursor mRNA sequences from 72 vertebrates and transferable downstream use.","evidence_snippet":"pre-trained on the precursor messenger RNA sequences of 72 vertebrates; capable of generating embeddings; MLM task may also play a role similar to MSA; unsupervised learning with genomic sequences of multiple species; pre-trained language model for pre-mRNA sequences to study and improve sequence-based prediction of RNA splicing"},{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_001784","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"SpliceBERT is presented as a pre-trained language model for pre-mRNA splicing, but the provided evidence supports unsupervised representation learning and embeddings rather than an explicitly generative architecture. It does provide foundation-model-like evidence through pretraining on precursor mRNA sequences from 72 vertebrates and transferable downstream use.","evidence_snippet":"pre-trained on the precursor messenger RNA sequences of 72 vertebrates; capable of generating embeddings; MLM task may also play a role similar to MSA; unsupervised learning with genomic sequences of multiple species; pre-trained language model for pre-mRNA sequences to study and improve sequence-based prediction of RNA splicing"}]}
