./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0220.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003361","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a new pre-training framework for cell identity understanding, but the described architecture is a cell encoder plus text encoder with cross-attention and matching probability, not a generative model. It does show foundation-model-like pretraining and transfer across downstream tasks.","evidence_snippet":"\"two trainable parts: a cell encoder and a text encoder\"; \"pre-training framework\"; \"zero-, few-shot, and full-data cell-type annotation tasks\"; \"initialized using PubMedBERT\"; \"pre-trained Geneformer\"; \"pre-trained language models (PLMs)\"; \"selfsupervised learning methods like masked modeling\"; \"calculate the matching probability\"; \"benchmark datasets\"; \"professional-level textual annotations\"; \"cross-modal knowledge\"; \"trained only on a single modality\"; \"fine-tuned for downstream tasks\"; \"assembled a set of benchmark datasets\"; \"pre-training dataset named scLibrary\"; \"unified representation of single-cell data and natural language\"; \"does not generate\"; \"matching probability p c,t\"; \"cell encoder\"; \"text encoder\"; \"Cell identity\"; \"downstream tasks\"; \"broad applicability\"; \"transferable representations\"; \"pre-training phase\"; \"initialized using PubMedBERT\"; \"pre-trained Geneformer\"; \"fine-tuned to adeptly perform diverse downstream tasks\"; \"crossattention module\"; \"unimodal text encoding\"; \"multimodal encoding\"; \"similarity function\"; \"cosine similarity\"; \"embedding sequence\"; \"joint embedding\"; \"text enriched with cell identity information\"; \"model performance on different downstream tasks\"; \"cell type annotation\"; \"single-cell integration tasks\"; \"cell pathway identification\"; \"NSCLC subtype classification\"; \"professional-level textual annotations\"; \"cell identity understanding\"; \"pre-trained language models\"; \"transcriptomics data\"; \"cross-modal knowledge\"; \"cell-text matching probability\""},{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003361","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a new pre-training framework for cell identity understanding, but the described architecture is a cell encoder plus text encoder with cross-attention and matching probability, not a generative model. It does show foundation-model-like pretraining and transfer across downstream tasks.","evidence_snippet":"Our model consists of two trainable parts: a cell encoder and a text encoder. We propose ... pre-training framework ... initialize our cell encoder ... initialized using PubMedBERT ... used for zero-, few-shot, and full-data cell-type annotation tasks ... calculate the matching probability p c,t between single-cell and text data."}]}
