sm\"; \"standard set of amino acids tokens\"; \"new PTM tokens\"; \"PTM-aware protein language model\"; \"bio modality present\"; \"text component absent\"; \"text-bio bridge absent\"; \"generative status unclear\"; \"foundation model evidence yes\"; \"EC2_no_text_component\"; \"biological_token_only_boundary\""}]}
./data/living_catalog_updates/update_2026-08-09/09_fulltext_screening_failed_complete_batch_retries_2026-08-11/role_logs/scope_reviewer/batch_0002.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000076","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Raygun is a primary generative protein-design method, but the evidence is entirely protein-sequence/PLM based. No natural-language text component or substantive text-bio bridge is described.","evidence_snippet":"Protein language models generate informative per-residue representations; Raygun implements this representation within an auto-encoder operating on ESM-2 embeddings"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000082","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"Unify is a transfer-learning framework for scRNA-seq integration that combines RNA expression with precomputed language-model embeddings. The text side is used as external embeddings, not as a substantive text-bio generative model.","evidence_snippet":"combining RNA expression with embeddings from protein language models and general-purpose language models"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000106","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"scMIR is presented as a vision-language foundation model with paired microscopy images and textual captions. The text-guided alignment is central to the model, so this is within scope.","evidence_snippet":"trained on paired single-cell images and structured textual captions to enable text-guided visual representation learning"},{"record_id":"update_2026-08-09__rec_000131","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"CellDuality is a primary LLM-based biological reasoning method: it defines biological tasks, constructs textual prompts, and trains the model to generate textual responses. The text-biology bridge is explicit and central.","evidence_snippet":"All inputs to the LLM are constructed as textual prompts x; The model's output is a textual response y"}]}
