./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:695:./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0143.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"july_update_2026-07-06__rec_000046","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract and full text describe HoloCell as a generative foundation model, pretrained on 468M single-cell profiles and used for transferable representation learning across modalities. The model explicitly supports cross-modal generation via iterative diffusion and remasking.","evidence_snippet":"“first generative foundation model”; “pretrained on ... 468 million single-cell profiles”; “cross-modal generation via iterative diffusion and remasking” [abstract] / “bidirectional iterative diffusion generation framework” [conclusion] / “large-scale ... pretraining” [data_representation] / “transferable representations” [discussion] .\",\"evidence_for_text_component\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_text_bio_bridge\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_generative_model\":\"“cross-modal generation via iterative diffusion and remasking” / “bidirectional iterative diffusion generation framework”\",\"boundary_case\":\"clear_include\"}]}]}"}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:704:./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0082.stderr.log:123:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_002483","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper presents PGL as a new generative model, not a wrapper or benchmark, and explicitly states autoregressive synthesis of full single-cell transcriptomes from metadata. It also claims broad training over ~14 million cells and positions the model as a foundational tool for in silico single-cell biology.","evidence_snippet":"PGL ... uses a large language model to synthesize complete single-cell RNA-seq profiles from metadata alone; ... autoregressively generate such sequences conditioned solely on cell-level metadata; training corpus comprised approximately 14 million cells from 2,118 datasets"}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:705:./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0086.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_002581","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract presents CellReasoner as a 7B large language model with chain-of-thought reasoning that generates cell type labels from gene expression profiles. It also reports zero- and few-shot generalization, which is foundation-model-like evidence.","evidence_snippet":"“large language model (LLM) tailored for single-cell type annotation”; “using only 380 high-quality chain-of-thought exemplars”; “directly maps cell-level gene expression profiles to cell type labels” ; “zero- and few-shot generalization”,"},{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_002581","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The abstract and full text describe a generative reasoning model that produces labels and explicit reasoning chains from gene-expression inputs. The model is positioned as a broadly generalizable LLM rather than a narrow predictor.","evidence_snippet":"“generate a cell type label directly”; “requiring an explicit reasoning chain”; “expert-level, marker-by-marker reasoning”,"}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:725:./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0028.stderr.log:124:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000950","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The provided full text explicitly calls Chroma a generative model and says it can generate new and diverse proteins across a broad array of structures and properties. It also describes broad programmability, including user-specified properties and free-text descriptions.","evidence_snippet":"“Chroma, a generative model that can generate new and diverse proteins across a broad array of structures and properties” and “accept descriptions of desired properties as free text”"},{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000950","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The provided full text explicitly calls Chroma a generative model and says it can generate new and diverse proteins across a broad array of structures and properties. It also describes broad programmability, including user-specified properties and free-text descriptions.","evidence_snippet":"“Chroma, a generative model that can generate new and diverse proteins across a broad array of structures and properties” and “accept descriptions of desired properties as free text”"}]}
