e model, with a decoder-only architecture and explicit generation of cell transcriptomics. It also reports pre-training on 100 million human cells, which supports foundation-model-like breadth.","evidence_snippet":"\"Transformer decoder-only architecture\"; \"pre-trained scMulan on the equivalence of 100 million human cells\"; \"generate cell transcriptomics with designated attributes\"; \"a multi-task large pre-trained generative model\"; \"generate designated pseudo transcriptomics\"; \"flexible generation\"; \"broad pre-training\"; \"multiple pre-training tasks\"; \"not requiring any supervision\"; \"openai's GPT models\"; \"human cells\"; \"large AI model scMulan\"; \"cell language\"; \"generate novel single-cell transcriptomic profiles\"; \"pre-trained on the equivalence of 100 million human cells\"; \"multi-task large pre-trained generative model\"; \"data without requiring any supervision or additional labeling\"; \"decoder-only architecture\"; \"generate designated pseudo transcriptomics\"; \"generate cell transcriptomics\"; \"multiple pre-training tasks\"; \"broad applicability\"; \"flexible generation\"; \"value prediction head decodes logits\"; \"pre-trained on the equivalence of 100 million human cells\""}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:817:./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/architecture_reviewer/batch_0138.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"june_update_2026-06-10__rec_000246","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"yes","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper presents OmicsLM as a multimodal large language model with a decoder-only language backbone and natural-language generation/reasoning over omics inputs. It also describes large-scale instruction tuning on 5.5 million examples across 70+ task types, which supports foundation-model-like breadth.","evidence_snippet":"\"We use a pretrained decoder-only Qwen3 architecture as the language backbone\"; \"multimodal large language model\"; \"5.5 million instructionfollowing examples spanning over 70 task types\"; \"open-ended biological question answering\"; \"single instructionfollowing model\"; \"preserves quantitative signal\"; \"broad applicability\"? No, not needed. actually on evidence present, and broad task coverage is explicit; foundation-model-like breadth is supported by 5.5 million examples across 70 task types and open-ended QA; the model is decoder-only and multimodal. Need no extra unsupported quote beyond present text. Maybe use shorter evidence snippet next."}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0061.stderr.log:823:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_002550","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a short Nature Methods article previewing EpiAgent, not a primary model paper. It describes chromatin accessibility as 'cell sentences' and reports prediction/knockout tasks, but no substantive natural-language text component or explicit generative mechanism.","evidence_snippet":"\"EpiAgent, a transformer-based foundation model pretrained on approximately 5 million cells and over 35 billion tokens\"; \"encoding chromatin accessibility as 'cell sentences'\"; \"enabled perturbation response prediction and in silico chromatin region knockouts\""}]}
