./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0003.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000323","paper_type":"application_wrapper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The record describes a new genomics method that repurposes a pre-trained LLM with a CNN embedder and a linear predictor, but the candidate model is trained and evaluated as supervised prediction, not generation. Text-lm and DNA alignment are explicit, so the text component and bridge are present, but the lack of a generative mechanism makes it out of scope.","evidence_snippet":"\"adapts a pre-trained LLM architecture for genomics\"; \"transformer layers from a pre-trained language model\"; \"minimizes the modality gap between DNA embeddings and language embeddings\"; \"fine-tuned on task-specific data in a supervised manner\"; \"linear predictor\"; \"repurposing existing LLMs for genomics tasks\"; \"achieves superior performance... on genomics benchmarks\"; \"cross-modal transfer in genomics\"; \"in a supervised manner\"; \"to identify significant transcription factor motifs\"; \"not requiring extensive pre-training on DNA sequence data\"; \"distribution distance between language embeddings and DNA embeddings\"; \"pre-trained language models\"; \"language models originally developed for NLP can be repurposed for seemingly unrelated domains like genomics\"; \"multiple genomics tasks\"; \"DNA sequence data\""}]}
