LSWARM, rather than a review or wrapper. It is centered on tumor microenvironment cell simulation and uses an LLM as the cognitive core of the cell agents.","evidence_snippet":"\"replaces rule-based cell decision-making with large language model (LLM)-driven autonomous agents\"; \"recapitulates TNBC microenvironment composition\"; \"Each cell in CELLSWARM is modeled as an autonomous agent\"; \"LLM serving as its cognitive core\"; \"structured knowledge bases for cancer-specific context\"; \"LLM-driven cell agents\"; \"cell-level agents in tumor microenvironment simulations\"; \"weights are cell-type-specific and defined in the Pathway Knowledge Base\"; \"sensing of indirect genetic perturbations\"; \"cancer-specific context\"; \"direct checkpoint knockouts\"; \"IFNγ knockout experiment\"; \"tumor microenvironment\""},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003902","paper_type":"application_wrapper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"application_wrapper","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"The paper presents an LLM-driven simulation framework rather than a new generative text-bio model. The candidate contribution is a wrapper that uses an LLM as the cognitive core for cell agents and demonstrates downstream simulation behavior.","evidence_snippet":"“replaces rule-based cell decision-making with large language model (LLM)-driven autonomous agents” and “LLM serving as its cognitive core”"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"application_wrapper","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"}}}]
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0043.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"july_update_2026-07-06__rec_000050","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a primary empirical study of biological reasoning models, not a review, benchmark, or wrapper. The record explicitly links natural-language task descriptions to molecular representations, but it does not explicitly state a generative mechanism such as decoder or autoregressive generation.","evidence_snippet":"none"},{"record_id":"july_update_2026-07-06__rec_000050","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"yes","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"none","uncertainty_reason":"generative_status_unclear","decision_rationale":"This is a primary empirical study of biological reasoning models, not a review, benchmark, or wrapper. The record explicitly links natural-language task descriptions to molecular representations, but it does not explicitly state a generative mechanism such as decoder or autoregressive generation.","evidence_snippet":"none"}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0074.stdout.log:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_003265","paper_type":"review_editorial","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"yes","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"unclear","foundation_model_evidence":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"review_editorial","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a tutorial/review-style paper rather than a primary model paper: it says, 'In this tutorial, we will explore the application of large language models.' It covers biomedical text and biological sequences, but does not present a new text-bio model or generative bridge.","evidence_snippet":"\"In this tutorial, we will explore the application of large language models\"; \"biomedical literature and health records presented as text\"; \"biological sequences or sequencing data arranged in sequences\"; \"brain signals as time series\""}]}
