e top 2,000 highly variable genes per cell\"; \"cell type identification\"; \"Benchmarking Dataset descriptions\"; no natural-language text, prompts, or descriptions are shown in the provided sections"}]}
./data/screening_codex_fulltext_2026-07-09/role_logs/adjudicator/batch_0016.response.txt:1:{"results":[{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_001487","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary single-cell transcriptomic model, but the only text-like element is a biological token sequence described as a sentence analogy. No substantive natural-language text, text-bio bridge, or generative mechanism is evidenced.","evidence_snippet":"\"representing single-cell transcriptomes as ordered sequences of gene names, analogous to sentences in text\"; \"converted into a 'cell sentence'\"; \"fine-tuned directly on single-cell data for age prediction\"; \"pretrained language models\"; \"the model can also identify genes whose modulation decreases predicted transcriptional age\"; \"[truncated]\"; \"leverages already well-validated LLMs\"; \"foundation models that must be trained from scratch on omics data\"; \"state-of-the-art accuracy in predicting biological age\"; \"model learns a universal latent representation of aging\"; \"not natural language text\"}]}ួ】"}]}
