also known as BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers) [ devlin2018bert ] has been employed. The model is dependent on both directions of the input (unlike autoregressive models that are only dependent on the previous words/tokens). In this study, a cell, denoted as X and characterized by a sequence of genes, undergoes a process to generate its corrupted counterpart, ˜ X . This corruption involves the random masking of the proportion r of its genes. This procedure can be equivalently conceptualized as independently and randomly masking each gene within the sequence.\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nThe task of MLM (Masked Language Modeling) is to reconstruct the expression values of masked genes based on the known genes. The corrupted version is then fed into the Transformer model.\n\nThe Transformer models is decomposed of L layers of Transformer blocks H θ :\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nThe Transformer block takes an input of length T , and outputs the same size in the output: 406\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nIn which H θ is the composition of the following functions: 407\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nLayerNorm and FeedForward are the usual layers used in modern neural networks. MultiHead function is the multi-head attention module that is defined as follows\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\n<!-- formula-not-decoded -->\n\nwhere Concat ( . ) is the concatenation function, and the diag ( . [truncated]","original_chars":5451},{"section_type":"data_representation","heading":"Methods","heading_level":2,"line_start":807,"line_end":1142,"text":"In this section, we will provide an overview of the PolyGene architecture and key features. Previous works [ yang2022scbert , theodoris2023transfer , cui2024scgpt ] on gene expression data from scRNA-seq data have been limited to statistical analysis of a large number of genes, for example, clustering and cell type annotation. This approach mirrors the pre-2010 natural language processing (NLP) research, which primarily focused on clustering, classification, topic modeling, and other statistical analyses. However, the advent of word embedding catalyzed a shift towards more granular text analyses, such as Named Entity Recognition (NER), sentiment analysis, and semantic interpretation [ mikolov2013distributed ]. We advocate for a parallel methodological evolution in genomics, leveraging the exponential growth in genetic data availability across various species. Concurrently, the integration of advanced machine learning frameworks, notably the Transformer architecture's success in NLP and related domains, has paved the way for analogous applications in genetics.\n\nIt's been known for a long time that there is a connection between genes in cells in terms of a network also known as Gene Regulatory Network (GRN). Despite this, research in this domain has predominantly been theoretical, with rudimentary models like Stuart A. [truncated]","original_chars":16311}],"docling_markdown":"data/docling_uncertain_no_vlm_2026-07-08/markdown/full_2026_07_06_rec_000405.md","first_pass_outputs":{"scope_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000405","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","primary_exclusion_code":"EC2_no_text_component","uncertainty_reason":"none","decision_rationale":"This is a primary model paper on scRNA-seq / human transcriptomics, but the model operates on gene-expression sequences rather than natural-language text. The selected sections describe BERT/MLM over masked genes and a genotype-phenotype manifold, not a substantive text-bio bridge.","evidence_snippet":"“single-cell RNA sequencing”; “a cell ... characterized by a sequence of genes”; “The task of MLM ... reconstruct the expression values of masked genes” , “multimodal foundation model” , “language models” , “BERT” , “genotype-phenotype relationship”"},"architecture_reviewer":{"record_id":"full_2026-07-06__rec_000405","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes","primary_exclusion_code":"EC3_not_generative","uncertainty_reason":"mixed_signals","decision_rationale":"The full text describes a BERT-based masked-language denoiser that reconstructs masked gene expression values, which is encoder-only MLM rather than an explicit generative decoder/autoregressive model. The paper does present a multimodal foundation model for genotype-phenotype analysis, but the generative mechanism is not established.","evidence_snippet":"\"BERT (Bidirectional Encoder Representations from Transformers)\" and \"The task of MLM is to reconstruct the expression values of masked genes\"; abstract says \"multimodal foundation model\" and \"genotype-phenotype relationship manifold\" for human transcriptomics, evidence_for_text_component\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_text_bio_bridge\":\"not_assessed\",\"evidence_for_generative_model\":\"BERT denoiser; MLM reconstruct the expression values of masked genes\",\"boundary_case\":\"generative_boundary\"}]} }</final>  જોકેassistant to=web.run  天天中彩票怎么json  荣富  天天中彩票qq{"},"python_gate":{"provisional_decision":"ADJUDICATE","provisional_code":"EC2_no_text_component","adjudication_reason":"criterion_unclear_or_reviewer_conflict","paper_type":"primary_model_paper","bio_modality_present":"yes","text_component_present":"no","text_bio_bridge_present":"no","generative_model_present":"no","foundation_model_evidence":"yes"}}}]
